# Build & Validation Rules

## 🚨 CRITICAL: Always Build After Changes

**Every code change MUST be validated with a successful build before committing.**

## Mandatory Build Command

```bash
npm run build
```

This command:
1. Compiles TypeScript (validates types)
2. Builds Next.js application
3. Checks for build errors
4. Validates all imports and dependencies

### What Build Catches

- ✅ TypeScript type errors
- ✅ Missing dependencies
- ✅ Import errors
- ✅ Invalid configurations
- ✅ Module resolution issues
- ✅ Circular dependencies
- ✅ Build-time optimizations

## Pre-Commit Validation Workflow

### Required Steps (In Order)

```bash
# 1. Format and lint check
npm run check

# 2. Build validation (CRITICAL)
npm run build

# 3. Run tests (if applicable)
npm run test:e2e:ci

# 4. If all pass, commit
git add .
git commit -m "Your commit message"
```

### Automated Pre-Commit Hook

Already configured via Husky in @.husky/pre-commit:

```bash
#!/bin/sh
. "$(dirname "$0")/_/husky.sh"

# Run lint-staged
npx lint-staged

# Note: Add build check here if needed
# npm run build
```

## Build Validation Checklist

Before committing any changes:

- [ ] Code compiles without TypeScript errors
- [ ] All imports resolve correctly
- [ ] No missing dependencies
- [ ] Build completes successfully
- [ ] No build warnings (or documented if acceptable)
- [ ] Bundle size is reasonable
- [ ] No circular dependencies introduced

